From 4a797502dc8fcdd101e3fa5c9123e84094c960db Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ajensenwaud <ajensenwaud@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 02:36:07 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 12/26] ling: kernel-contract gates 1-4 for the last four Ling
 launches: tf_ling_chunks_r16 (576-wide q and keys over a linear cache,
 through tf_glm_merge), tf_exl3_plan_finish_after (gate-up with and without
 the limit, fp32 down), the Ling-order FP8 gate-up decode and prompt instances
 (with and without the limit). The FP8 twin's clamps compare, so a NaN stays
 NaN as in torch.clamp (finite bits unchanged; decode instance 155 -> 156
 registers on sm_120/121, records updated for nvcc 13.0 and 13.3)

---
 docs/kernel-contract.md                       |   6 +-
 zig/kernels/cuda/experts.cuh                  |   6 +-
 zig/src/core/contract/ling_cuda_records.zig   |   2 +-
 .../contract/measurements/pending_133.zig     |   2 +-
 zig/tests/cuda/contract_ling.zig              |   5 +-
 zig/tests/cuda/contract_ling_fp8.zig          | 220 ++++++++
 zig/tests/cuda/contract_ling_more.zig         | 481 ++++++++++++++++++
 7 files changed, 714 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 zig/tests/cuda/contract_ling_fp8.zig
